     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Discussed Jerry's work thus far:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://github.com/JerryPan/fcrepo/tree/fcrepo-954"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://github.com/JerryPan/fcrepo/tree/fcrepo-954",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "...at today's committer meeting:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FCREPO/2011-09-27+-+Committer+Meeting"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FCREPO/2011-09-27+-+Committer+Meeting",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "(see notes on above page) There was agreement that we should recommend new configurations/dependencies for modules come in through spring config files instead of the old way, fedora.fcfg. Also, we discussed that a utility to do the conversion on a per-module basis (FCFG to spring config file) would be good. So ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-1001#icft=FCREPO-1001"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": " was created.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Scoping this for 3.6 since it now seems likely that the work & tests will be ready in time for the release.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
